\name{RSDynamicHash}
\alias{RSDynamicHash}
\title{RSDynamicHash: Mutable, Hash-Based Key-Value Container}
\description{
\code{RSDynamicHash} is a hash-table-like mutable data structure for storing uniquely
identifiable \code{RSObject} instances. Keys are derived from each object’s \code{hash()} method,
and equivalence is determined by \code{isEqual()}. The structure dynamically resizes
when the load factor exceeds 75\%.

Unlike \code{RSMutableSet} or \code{RSMutableDictionary}, this class stores objects \strong{as-is};
it does not call \code{copy()} upon insertion. This allows full control over the
mutability and lifecycle of stored objects, and is suitable for internal frameworks
requiring high-performance mutable object indexing.
}
